Lays out right-to-left text in the right order when a style's font-faces send
it through HarfBuzz. The HarfBuzz path shaped every run left to right, skipped
the bidi reordering that glyph PBFs get, and received ICU's Arabic presentation
forms instead of the letters, so Arabic and Kurdish labels came out reversed and
unjoined. Now each run of one direction is shaped in that direction, the runs
come in visual order, and only glyph PBF sections take presentation forms.
Adapted from the patch that yusfrubar-sketch posted on the upstream issue.
Issue: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/issues/4513
Upstream: not proposed

